JX-TEX-N-31\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(12959.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(13810.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(14866.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(15255.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(15755.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16577.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(17577.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(18077.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(18466.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Therefore, the dark fringe forms at O.</p>\n<p>Hence, option (A) is correct.</p>\n<p>The shape of wavefronts from both sources for D &gt;&gt; d is semi-circular, which are concentric with each other with the difference just in their phase resulting in concentric semicircular interference fringes. That is, the region nearby point O is dark.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Wave Optics Question 18 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0rab3wv/20df9477-e2b8-4bb2-8aa3-8eac71cf9364/17b4f1f0-a3e7-11ec-9889-8ff85cf85963/file-1l0rab3ww.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Hence, option (B) is correct.</p>\n","exam":"jee-advanced","questions":[{"question_id":"while-conducting-the-youngs-double-slit-experiment-a-stude-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-9i6bopiubi67tixn","qKey":"while-conducting-the-youngs-double-slit-experiment-a-stude-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-9i6bopiubi67tixn","permalink":"while-conducting-the-youngs-double-slit-experiment-a-stude-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-9i6bopiubi67tixn","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline","year":2016,"subject":"physics","chapter":"wave-optics","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"content":"While conducting the Young's double slit experiment, a student replaced the two slits with a large opaque plate in the XY-plane containing two small holes that act as two coherent point sources (S<sub>1</sub>, S<sub>2</sub>) emitting light of wavelength 600 mm. The student mistakenly placed the screen parallel to the XZ-plane (for z &gt; 0) at a distance D = 3 m from the mid-point of S<sub>1</sub>S<sub>2</sub>, as shown schematically in the figure. The distance between the source d = 0.6003 mm. The origin O is at the intersection of the screen and the line joining S<sub>1</sub>S<sub>2</sub>.<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Wave Optics Question 18 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0no0py2/c766b740-a7e4-4506-a9a7-0eb7ca19cc3e/94096ba0-a1e9-11ec-8b25-4fc5294790d5/file-1l0no0py3.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 